diffs.patch:
Index: openwiki/.claims/architecture/overview.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/architecture/overview.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/architecture/overview.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,118 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:7db16811242a23970a55e4e01db5e954d86761b7c216f1eeb64c8ec3fd255c83",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_ac26c6204b014e3aaa33865a6312c4cc",
+      "statement": "The monorepo is organized around an OS analogy: packages/workshop-backend is the kernel that connects users to gadgets and gatekeepers while enforcing sandboxing and access control, packages/gatekeeper-* are the device drivers, and packages/workshop-frontend is the shell.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://README.md#L97-L108",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b20149b8e3b72f6b03a93c32e922871ea12d9800b1a3286474dacb1a0c046daa:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_42f27fadfb2c4272af329db55dbba052",
+      "statement": "Every workspace is its own Durable Object, every Gadget runs in a Dynamic Worker Facet, and Gatekeepers install facets into each workspace to manage access to remote services; the stack can also run entirely on the open-source workerd runtime (which is what pnpm run-local does under wrangler).",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://README.md#L116-L116",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d661977734f3f340f9f72aa5f02f49b470d20acda8e45db34d1beb99f754e07c:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_c16d12801e4e4891baef1f90312a15a4",
+      "statement": "The router Worker is a deployment's public origin and its routing config is its binding set: gatekeepers are discovered by scanning GATEKEEPER_* service bindings and mounted at /gatekeeper/<name>/*, while /api* and /blueprint-screenshot/* go to WORKSHOP_BACKEND and remaining paths go to frontend assets (falling through to the backend in dev).",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/router/src/index.ts#L1-L56",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c7c0f2979487f98a9badcb46718aaca6730929bbefea59c4aea330892c3245fa:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_f3b7b05a45a245bbabc2da35791b7ff3",
+      "statement": "The backend Worker's Durable Object classes are UserDurableObject, OverseerDurableObject, AdminSettings, and PendingLogin, declared via wrangler migrations and reached dynamically through ctx.exports rather than an explicit durable_objects binding.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/wrangler.jsonc#L47-L63",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9a6f506793e9dd1f2a1fb6da151d2109f9a823d06b92860f26c102bfbb0aa7ca:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_52634bbda06f40fdaeb472194e4cab5b",
+      "statement": "Workshop-backend persists blueprint metadata in the BLUEPRINTS KV namespace, avatars in AVATARS KV, blueprint content in the BLUEPRINT_CONTENT R2 bucket, and loads gadget dynamic workers through the LOADER worker-loader binding.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/wrangler.jsonc#L66-L83",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:79e7e61e5c193344529291c07bd4410b8aceb41414627c22741a0a41cb412fda:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_0ea5b37e7ffb412cb67626db07d4abca",
+      "statement": "The backend enables the global_fetch_strictly_public compatibility flag so production fetch() is strictly internet-facing (an SSRF guard, notably for the webFetch agent tool), alongside allow_irrevocable_stub_storage and nodejs_compat for persistent stubs, provider SDKs, and Puppeteer PDF export.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/wrangler.jsonc#L11-L32",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d22f6a740fc35323cf8a0f82e8a0ad22495026dc29df5535473ea8488f7d8d3e:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_2c162a6bed75469d9051cbd2563e4927",
+      "statement": "The backend serves its RPC API only at the /api path: HTTP POST gets a Cap'n Web batch response (cross-origin allowed because the API uses in-band authorization), and a WebSocket upgrade opens a persistent session the server can abort via an AbortSignal-backed close.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/src/server.ts#L816-L868",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:04b8d6ced2375ec2382213831f1dc1f32f90257295f5f49e96fde65641447318:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/src/server.ts#L887-L902",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4705ca5c126ff85eb2bebb65eab485a77d223967132627e750fb1d478fd0412a:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_525badc1a58e44d7a4500a2d9906a860",
+      "statement": "A Gadget runs as two isolated sandboxes: server.js executes in a Dynamic Worker with internet access disabled, reaching outside only through injected bindings; client.js runs in a sandboxed iframe that talks to the server exclusively through a Cap'n Web RPC session established over postMessage.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://README.md#L160-L162",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fb402ad945f67e538f72ef0befd4334b059beb4210f65ed4353b13bfeabe3a56:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_df2cfdbf05194a5e901a955235a1a18b",
+      "statement": "The Overseer loads a gadget's running facet on demand through the LOADER binding with a cache key of workspace id + code version + gadget id, names facets per gadget, and defensively aborts/reloads a facet when it cannot confirm the running code state.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/src/overseer.ts#L3958-L4090",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2487e6847e18ae660e07f12b3598e35ebf0bc0e95e8a4077ad49c209fbd5d50a:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_ca3563080dfc4eb582798dbcd689de73",
+      "statement": "Service connectors follow a common object shape: a per-user UserAccount Durable Object holding the OAuth connection plus per-resource Gatekeeper Durable Object implementations (e.g. GitHubGatekeeperImpl) that expose the sandboxed session API.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/gatekeeper-github/src/github.ts#L1045-L1045",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c1a0ec2840665861ffbbdeb3e4239e36c1717119569c1c45299f770a3d0f9d63:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/gatekeeper-github/src/github.ts#L1382-L1382",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5e8d2cfa71a55da551ff0b0a2bcdad2549c919467a38eb9f9953c1972cf9bbec:"
+        }
+      ]
+    }
+  ],
+  "verification": {
+    "by": "openwiki/0.4.3",
+    "at": "2026-09-01T10:56:53.614Z"
+  }
+}

Index: openwiki/.claims/development/testing.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/development/testing.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/development/testing.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,158 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:9a10ec80858611ee541e41340a69e16d5e9f1d9a66666b63cb008c59a0c11bee",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_02297cdf8fd141aeb186a4b6752dec3d",
+      "statement": "pnpm test runs the root scripts suite via node --test first, then the per-package cached test tasks via vp run with the root package excluded by an explicit --filter '!cloudflare-os' to avoid running the root suite twice.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://package.json#L10-L10",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a1cd587457cb85cc0e5768222c798e5a891b4611fc090205a9067c1450a9c64a:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_3e3baa9c142b42bc9aae4807ebce32a8",
+      "statement": "Per-package vitest runs are declared as Vite+ tasks rather than package.json scripts so the task's input can exclude vitest's scratch paths; direct uncached runs use the test:run script because tasks and scripts may not share a name.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://scripts/vitest-task-vite-config.ts#L14-L19",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:41ace801e004a58f9b0aa2bd6f9b77080dc1f77d20cb1e3226de80f12e479480:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_56302ccb1165422f838a020ea6ee9b8b",
+      "statement": "Test-task fingerprinting excludes node_modules/.vite, node_modules/.vite-temp and .wrangler at workspace scope because vp refuses to cache a command that reads paths it also writes, and package-relative exclusions would let sibling packages invalidate each other.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://scripts/vitest-task-vite-config.ts#L41-L69",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a5271351f5f26eca5f8d86b2507a37dcb34ba88087ad7088f268af66f4b223db:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_570ac07e6e524cbf9c728e9385704c49",
+      "statement": "Every test-task command runs under with-timeout.ts with a 60s idle and 600s total watchdog that kills the entire process tree and exits 124, because vitest's own timeouts die with a crashed workerd child and vp has no task timeout.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://scripts/vitest-task-vite-config.ts#L70-L124",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a0e68e84f003cfc69ca94f1e1b9ea5d97f228a4a6d0e3ce224f22378bb41ef25:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://scripts/with-timeout.ts#L1-L30",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0892c4ed1f34e674b506cbd14c5dee11413145ad18a2f2908d092a60082bc407:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_976a55f062b444d8876785da148c889c",
+      "statement": "Packages whose tests target workerd load assert-workerd.ts as a setup file that throws unless navigator.userAgent is Cloudflare-Workers, turning a silently Node-fallen-back vitest-pool-workers run into a loud failure.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://scripts/assert-workerd.ts#L1-L15",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ddc7c5c4f95e062951de5b4757bde9f0d24bb2849b3253881b31b3ddf9f640e7:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_0b55a2d442934841870baaa57bb269b2",
+      "statement": "Integration suites boot real Workers under wrangler's createTestHarness with checked-in configs patched in memory and speak Cap'n Web over WebSocket to /api, stubbing only outbound HTTP — the code under test runs in another process.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/integration-testing.md#L24-L32",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8acf38f045e31f73a5b459d9bf5855af53c0f643be339caeace929a0f5d36ca5:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_23acc80d3bdc4cfea7e48d1ae48da6ae",
+      "statement": "Fake timers are unusable in the createTestHarness suites because the code under test reads workerd's out-of-process clock; they only work in in-isolate vitest-pool-workers unit tests.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/integration-testing.md#L34-L42",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:05d774ea5498b57f66d3fdce76da83c926cd0499801d4eb5a68511b1ca768ff0:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_3c3410238536443eba5747b93e8a6d11",
+      "statement": "The NetworkInterceptor passes loopback through and throws on any fetch no handler matched, making an unmocked vendor call a test failure rather than real internet access.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/integration-tests/src/network-interceptor.ts#L1-L26",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:921f0467accfa6e587b12bc99e58e9c0fd3348958432406dd05ee1639b30a73f:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_44870502c797488695f108f8fcb44bff",
+      "statement": "Integration tests share one harness with persistent storage (server.reset costs ~3s and is a teardown, not a wipe), take fresh identities per test, and assert the nothing-escaped condition in afterAll because afterEach would race concurrent siblings.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/integration-testing.md#L67-L83",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:13474194c020726d88f5a255a4d742e09500507e44b16562c3645e157348b7a2:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_c7351741f6794858af6e75f3ff950cc9",
+      "statement": "The fixture gatekeeper exists because overseer observer tests need on-command refusal that shipping gatekeepers can only produce at prohibitive cost, and adding test hooks to them was rejected as circular; per-vendor coverage remains the intended trajectory via pluggable handlers.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/integration-testing.md#L44-L63",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2957bc6f2e3fa3a520c78cc981409353b5cd418a06f1ce8fbcb7aa4f24b198b9:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_ac88fab6d9774853a14d6639fbd0a559",
+      "statement": "Stubs in the integration toolkit must be minted via stubFor() and capnweb value-imports are lint-restricted to rpc-client.ts, because a vendoring repo can resolve two capnweb copies and a stub from the wrong one fails to serialize.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/integration-tests/src/rpc-client.ts#L65-L65",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ac900761ccd83aa7eb29b44a78bac67c211ce668793aad8a11a2e64fad181958:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://vite.config.ts#L158-L174",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8f9b11d18331f03810f7301ba5ff3abec16bf4f8ca1056e4e2db59db2e4d3d91:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_c95d1c4e72694e09800974f2b029480c",
+      "statement": "The pinned wrangler version is coupled to the root workerd override: a newer wrangler bundles a newer workerd than the override supplies and the test harness fails to boot with a compatibility-date mismatch.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/integration-testing.md#L85-L99",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ea85e82bfd098fe565e16b5319a19b90d8cc9cb4823ff5a7bd020d5bcbd30b6c:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_f50b9e2805ba4363917dbb008abc8ec7",
+      "statement": "Worker entry modules may export only classes and the default handler as values, because workerd turns every named value export into an entrypoint and rejects non-function map entries.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/integration-testing.md#L120-L128",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:80ffd62b350c153aa08cf55e18dc4aa9f296c85440a35693ce115b8c8188efc2:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_c3a4f24ef61d44ee82d95135b1a687cd",
+      "statement": "CI lint/build/test run on fork PRs, but preview deployments intentionally do not, since GitHub withholds the deploy secrets from fork-triggered runs.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://CONTRIBUTING.md#L13-L23",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:31951d0dfcb0372e6d099f599e3145d08a011a562ae5c20063f30cd4d97d2996:"
+        }
+      ]
+    }
+  ],
+  "verification": {
+    "by": "openwiki/0.4.3",
+    "at": "2026-09-01T10:56:53.614Z"
+  }
+}

Index: openwiki/.claims/gatekeepers/mcp-connectors.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/gatekeepers/mcp-connectors.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/gatekeepers/mcp-connectors.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,138 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:efad7df223c1c69525b5bcc4d60c28782788f4793fa0944c771d433205778a0a",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_e1a17b58276942d8a35e78b12a483408",
+      "statement": "mcp-shared is a library (not a Worker) holding the code whose duplication would become a security disagreement — tool classification, scope grammar, OAuth lifecycle, approval wiring — while each connector keeps its own entrypoint, DOs, connect form, and configurator, varying shared behavior only through named hooks.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/mcp-shared/README.md#L1-L19",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3c887262ae17718a9efb75149ec09e8f82eedf1fb3e8d33db218ec5a4f648bad:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_a40228f1a793429c944915d3a4207d1d",
+      "statement": "tools.ts is the trust boundary: nothing outside it reads tool annotations, and a deployment-level ServerTrust tier (byo vs vetted, read fresh at each use) decides how far a server's self-description is believed.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/mcp-shared/src/tools.ts#L1-L34",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bf7c0e3c0fb64db469374dbd827db234dad080c385d6a082381361e2dbc8ac70:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_db5528aa14294d3aa161359466e3ca4c",
+      "statement": "readOnlyHint === true classifies a tool as an observation on both tiers, while auto-applying a write additionally requires a vetted endpoint with destructiveHint === false and idempotentHint === true; all comparisons are === true/=== false so unannotated tools default to queued actions.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/mcp-shared/src/tools.ts#L56-L80",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fbb84d23022528dee0048981d6963bf1b7553b32c0c6c54d43bd1ba4d32d40f5:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_184cc072a3ed4ca68a2bc5651ef8d33c",
+      "statement": "The user-pasted connector is always tier byo, and the portal connector defaults to byo, becoming vetted only when the admin sets MCP_PORTAL_TRUST_ANNOTATIONS=true — because a portal aggregates upstream servers whose annotations the administrator never saw.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/gatekeeper-mcp-portal/src/config.ts#L40-L40",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:eae39afcd843dafc9996be13c065579f7d52ce62fd669e4efcd4fa262d8a3223:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/gatekeeper-mcp/src/mcp.ts#L78-L78",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c6f306efafa1adb0cee2f584ceaca55606158093c08aef87c580aca5f697755f:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_31bb356d0b7b4e7ebb6d74b96a40706c",
+      "statement": "An MCP grant is encoded in the resource URL fragment — whole endpoint, #server=<name>, exact #tool names, or server-plus-tool combinations — with wire tool names stored absolutely so pre-portal grants resolve identically, and this fragment is what the user approved, what describe shows, and what the facet enforces.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/mcp-shared/src/scope.ts#L1-L10",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:668441cc50e06c6814479250d7dd6c7602f8ae32e4eef7c7a17e265cf5908c27:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_9ed4ff6e1ce94d8393d43db93c2ed99c",
+      "statement": "MCP bindings are owner-only: addObserver refuses unconditionally because same-origin authentication proves identity, not permission to see what the gadget read on the owner's credentials, while writes remain allowed.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/mcp-shared/src/sharing-policy.ts#L1-L5",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fde614630e70088cc41d47f591b581d763877dccd4d68e85a4d5a61c81e23e8c:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_7cc91d16f799458b85074d8306118522",
+      "statement": "One McpSession implementation is the single path every gadget tool call takes, identical for both connectors; per-connector differences arrive only through the McpSessionHost seam and the base never touches DO state or credentials.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/mcp-shared/src/session.ts#L1-L5",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7c85cd26b728128a7f667cc9fbc62bec603ed2be203bc7e070699622c5ccc213:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_1e1db137638c4ea1985805d244c429bc",
+      "statement": "Approval-gated MCP calls have a Durable lifecycle in the owning facet's isolated SQLite with claims persisted before external I/O (so an interrupted write is never replayed) and bounded result, argument, pending, and retention sizes.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/mcp-shared/src/action-store.ts#L1-L10",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4a3c396806151deee3d507bbb78dae05b5710978c73458bcb8af5caa2537cc30:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_8d301aab54fe4530991069d55d9af995",
+      "statement": "All outbound requests follow redirects by hand, re-validating each hop and dropping Authorization on cross-origin hops, because fetch's default redirect-following would let a validated server escape to blocklisted hosts after every check had run.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/mcp-shared/src/fetch.ts#L1-L8",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ecaf6fbda13db23de161258998ec751d3dcd25ce4232bbd021fe539e0ef9c94d:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_fa67f89f9f114400b01f53f79721657d",
+      "statement": "Every SDK OAuth operation receives fetchFn: sdkFetch(...) so SDK requests and their redirects retain endpoint and SSRF checks.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/mcp-shared/src/account.ts#L527-L527",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a13a8a864ae04b8dd6ca8fd043b0c4909772a290a6cff3124eeb98bb1c96322c:"
+        },
